# Trivy suppressions.
#
# Each entry needs a reason it is not exploitable here — not just that a fix is
# inconvenient. Revisit whenever the dependency tree around it changes.

# CVE-2026-93687 — braces: stack exhaustion (DoS) from deeply nested patterns.
#
# No fix exists: the advisory covers every published version (`range: "*"`, latest
# is 3.0.3, released 2024-05-21), so there is no upgrade to take. It reaches the
# image only through tailwindcss@3 -> micromatch/chokidar -> braces.
#
# Not exploitable here:
#  - tailwindcss@3 is a runtime dependency of packages/email (its renderer loads
#    @bchatsign/tailwind-config, whose index.cjs requires tailwindcss/defaultTheme),
#    so it cannot be demoted to devDependencies to drop the chain.
#  - Nothing in the app calls micromatch, chokidar or braces directly, and the
#    patterns those tools expand are internal globs, never user input — the DoS
#    needs an attacker-supplied pattern.
#  - braces is not in the server bundle (apps/remix/build/server).
#
# Remove this once tailwindcss 4 removes the micromatch/chokidar dependency.
CVE-2026-93687
